version nibble is zero.

The casts are explicit-only and stay installed so migration replays on fresh
databases keep working.

``CREATE CAST`` on built-in types requires owning the source or target type,
i.e. a superuser. When the migration user lacks that privilege (production),
a superuser must run BOOTSTRAP_SQL once beforehand; the migration then detects
the existing casts and skips itself.
"""

